From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:03:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] render: add composite_timing GPU timestamps per filter

Bracket each composite with timestamp queries while the composite_timing
log scope is at debug, read them back a few submits later so the queue
never stalls, and log the average per filter every two seconds.

A requested SGSR filter can fall back to FSR or use a cached image.
Label the pass that actually ran so these cases reach the right totals.
---
 src/rendervulkan.cpp | 218 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/rendervulkan.hpp |   5 +
 2 files changed, 223 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
index b31a034a..a691570b 100644
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <array>
 #include <bitset>
+#include <deque>
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include "vulkan_include.h"
 #include "Utils/Algorithm.h"
